camera-engine-rkaiq (6.32.0-2+rkr7.20251222.7fc7452) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * debian/rules: put libdrm's include directory on the search path, and drop
    the drm/ prefix from the two includes in the tree that carry one. rkaiq's
    CMake emits -DHAS_LIBDRM and no -I to go with it, so this only ever built
    because linux-libc-dev ships the kernel's own /usr/include/drm. bookworm's
    does not -- Debian restored those headers to it only after bookworm, and
    trixie's has 28 files there against bookworm's none -- so the build failed
    on xf86drm.h:40's #include <drm.h> and on rkaiq/xcore/drm_buffer.h:23's
    #include <drm/drm_fourcc.h>. libdrm-dev has both headers under
    /usr/include/libdrm on every suite, which is what pkg-config reports and
    what this package's Build-Depends already promises.
  * Same upstream commit as -1; this is a packaging-only change.

 -- Mixtile <dev@mixtile.com>  Wed, 09 Sep 2026 03:40:00 +0000

camera-engine-rkaiq (6.32.0-1+rkr7.20251222.7fc7452) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Built from mixtile-sdk-linux-external-camera_engine_rkaiq
    7fc74525d99691920a4e92bbfb4ac3a66d0dc554, the linux-6.1-stan-rkr7 branch
    of Mixtile's mirror of the Rockchip SDK.
  * The tree carries no debian/, so all of it is ours.
  * Two binary packages from one source, -rk3588 and -rk356x, because the
    libraries are compiled against one ISP register layout or the other:
    rkaiq/build/linux/envsetup.sh:60-89 maps rk3588 to ISP_HW_V30 and rk356x
    to ISP_HW_V21. They conflict and both Provides: camera-engine-rkaiq.
  * The tuning goes to /etc/iqfiles, where rkaiq_3A_server.cpp:33 looks for
    it, not to the share/iqfiles the CMake install writes -- upstream's
    install path and upstream's own hardcoded runtime path disagree.
  * rkaiq_3A_server has no install rule of its own upstream, although the
    SysV script that starts it does. We install the binary and ship a
    systemd unit in place of that script.

 -- Mixtile <dev@mixtile.com>  Tue, 08 Sep 2026 09:00:00 +0000
